{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "133", "x": 0.8951488575183035, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03859439108533224, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "F", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.01859382309708816, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Another concern is whether there may be unintended ecological effects of", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.7656877532814905, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "using guard dogs. Studies suggest that reducing deaths of one type of predator", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "may have a negative impact on other species. The extent of this problem isn't", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.8260335309911918, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "known, but the consequences are clear in Namibia. Cheetahs aren't the only", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8260745409727137, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "species that cause sheep and goat losses there: other predators also attack", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8259028116750906, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "livestock. In 2015, researchers reported that in spite of the impact farmers", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8260988393867654, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "obtaining guard dogs had on cheetahs, the number of jackals killed by dogs and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8262593934644238, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "people actually increased. Guard dogs have other ecological impacts too. They", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.8260771040965588, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "have been found to spread diseases to wild animals, including endangered", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.8260772066215126, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Ethiopian wolves. They may also compete with other carnivores for food. And by", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3780571491167385, "w": 0.8265414396123408, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "creating a 'landscape of fear', their mere presence can influence the behaviour of", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40638753691226864, "w": 0.82620782341266, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "prey animals.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4347178869864063, "w": 0.13973202847774127, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "G", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5111307907807106, "w": 0.021818989015784024, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "The evidence so far, however, indicates that these consequences aren't", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.5111307907807106, "w": 0.7656224448859169, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "always negative. Guard dogs can deliver unexpected benefits by protecting", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5394611408548482, "w": 0.8267980595717143, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "vulnerable wildlife from predators. For example, their presence has been found to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5677915286503784, "w": 0.8263386452537149, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "protect birds which build their nests on the ground in fields, where foxes would", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5961219164459085, "w": 0.8261860881224533, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "normally raid them. Indeed, Australian researchers are now using dogs to enhance", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6244523042414386, "w": 0.8268583442445515, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "biodiversity and create refuges for species threatened by predation. So if we can", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6527826543155762, "w": 0.8259247520152049, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "get this right, there may be a bright future for guard dogs in promoting", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6811501222399445, "w": 0.8260335309911918, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "harmonious coexistence between humans and wildlife.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7094804723140822, "w": 0.5594895149267618, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}